From 6911161c4fcb62fcb456cdd63c8ba7478a201149 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Gre=C5=84?= <witold.gren@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:50:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ws: siren on/off and the recordings of the SD card

siren takes on (and seconds, default 30, at most 900): the manual mode of reolink_aio (playMode 2, onOff 1/0), switched off by its timer unless a newer siren came; without on it sounds once as before. State siren_on.

The SD card: sd_recordings keeps the list of the card (searched in the background with refresh, a year back by the camera's calendar DayRecords 142, kept in <snapshot_dir>/sd/<camera>/list.json) with cover thumbnails (CoverPreview 298, or else the first I-frame of a replay of the sub stream file, as a JPEG served at GET /sd_thumbnail/{camera}/{day}/{file}.jpg); sd_sync copies chosen files or those of the last hours that the recording folder lacks, one after another in a queue; sd_auto copies the newest recording 5 minutes after each motion notification. Files land in <record_dir>/<camera>/<YYYY-MM-DD>/HHMMSS-HHMMSS.mp4 (written as .part, renamed once whole), the camera's frames muxed with their own times (a leap of the camera's clock is taken as one frame; the codec is read from the frames). One operation on a card at a time. Nothing on the card is deleted. [websocket] sd_stream = main (default) or sub.

Search: findAlarmVideo 272/273/274 (reolink_aio), and on 400/405 the older FileInfoList 14/15/16 with the host channel 250 in the header (the Reolink app; wire format from the nodelink-js captures). Download: by time 143/144, or for a file of the older search by replay 5 (message number 0, leftovers of an earlier replay left out) stopped by 7, ending when the data goes quiet.

Binary payloads with encryptLen keep their unencrypted rest (only the first encryptLen bytes are AES; the rest was cut off). Live views shorter than a second are not kept.
